" Tables: alignment (org-table-align) and field motion (TAB / S-TAB).

Given org (align: widths, numbers to the right, separator expanded, short rows filled):
  |Name|Qty|Note|
  |-
  | apple |  3 | red, crunchy |
  |kiwi|12|
  |ñandú| 1.5 |x|

Execute:
  call org#table#align()

Expect org:
  | Name  | Qty | Note         |
  |-------+-----+--------------|
  | apple |   3 | red, crunchy |
  | kiwi  |  12 |              |
  | ñandú | 1.5 | x            |

Given org (an Emacs-aligned table is left unchanged: links count as their description):
  | File     | Headline                           | Time   |
  |----------+------------------------------------+--------|
  |          | ALL *Total time*                   | *4:41* |
  |----------+------------------------------------+--------|
  | work.org | *File time*                        | *3:29* |
  |          | *[[file:/tmp/work.org::*Reunión semanal][Reunión semanal]]*                  | *1:12* |
  |          | *[[file:/tmp/work.org::*Plan][Plan del próximo trimestre largo]]* | *2:17* |

Execute:
  let before = getline(1, '$')
  call org#table#align()
  AssertEqual before, getline(1, '$')
  Assert !&modified

Given org (indented table keeps its indent; mostly-text column stays left):
  - list item
    |a|b|
    |1|x|

Execute:
  2
  call org#table#align()

Expect org:
  - list item
    | a | b |
    | 1 | x |

Given org (align keeps the cursor in its field):
  |a|bb|
  |ccc|d|

Execute:
  call cursor(2, 6)
  call org#table#align()
  AssertEqual [2, 9], [line('.'), col('.')]

" ── Field motion ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Given org (TAB goes to the next field, over separators, then opens a new row):
  | a | b |
  |---+---|
  | c | d |

Execute:
  call cursor(1, 3)
  call org#table#next_field()
  AssertEqual [1, 7], [line('.'), col('.')]
  call org#table#next_field()
  AssertEqual [3, 3], [line('.'), col('.')]
  call org#table#next_field()
  call org#table#next_field()
  AssertEqual ['| c | d |', '|   |   |'], getline(3, 4)
  AssertEqual [4, 3], [line('.'), col('.')]

Given org (S-TAB goes back, across rows and over separators):
  | a | b |
  |---+---|
  | c | d |

Execute:
  call cursor(3, 3)
  call org#fold#shifttab()
  AssertEqual [1, 7], [line('.'), col('.')]
  call org#table#prev_field()
  AssertEqual [1, 3], [line('.'), col('.')]
  call org#table#prev_field()
  AssertEqual [1, 3], [line('.'), col('.')]

Given org (normal-mode Tab on a table moves fields instead of folding):
  * H
  |x|y|

Execute:
  call cursor(2, 1)
  call org#fold#tab()
  AssertEqual ['| x | y |', 7], [getline(2), col('.')]

Given org (insert-mode Tab moves fields and keeps inserting):
  |a|b|
  |c|d|

Do:
  A\<Esc>0a\<Tab>X\<Tab>Y\<Esc>

Expect org:
  | a | Xb |
  | Yc | d  |

Given org (<C-c><C-c> on a table aligns it):
  |[[https://example.com][site]]|1|
  |longer text|22|

Execute:
  call cursor(2, 1)
  call org#dispatch#ctrl_c()

Expect org:
  | [[https://example.com][site]]        |  1 |
  | longer text | 22 |

Given org (outside a table, insert Tab chains to a global mapping like Codeium's):
  plain text
  |a|b|

Execute:
  " Codeium maps: imap <script><silent><nowait><expr> <Tab> codeium#Accept()
  function! FakeAccept() abort
    return 'ACCEPTED'
  endfunction
  " Mapped after this buffer's ftplugin ran, as Codeium does on VimEnter
  imap <silent><expr> <Tab> FakeAccept()

Do:
  A\<Tab>\<Esc>
  jA\<Tab>\<Esc>

Then:
  iunmap <Tab>
  AssertEqual ['plain textACCEPTED', '| a | b |', '|   |   |'], getline(1, '$')

Given org (with no other mapping, insert Tab outside a table is a plain Tab):
  text

Do:
  A\<Tab>x\<Esc>

Expect org:
  text	x
